  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/21-seahorses-and-pipefish/microphis-deocata-bred/",
      "html": "<p>Microphis deocata is probably the prettiest freshwater pipefish. Adults reach approximately 15 cm.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/21-seahorses-and-pipefish/microphis-deocata-bred/",
      "html": "<p>This pipefish is very sensitive to transport. It neither tolerates water deterioration nor can it starve for long. Due to its high demands, M. deocata is imported only very rarely. Habituation to frozen food succeeds only exceptionally and should never be regarded as possible when considering acquiring such animals.</p><p>Offspring of this species are usually not sold, but are passed on directly from the breeder to other enthusiasts.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/21-seahorses-and-pipefish/microphis-deocata-bred/",
      "html": "<p>India, where it lives in clear running waters at the foot of the Himalaya.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/21-seahorses-and-pipefish/microphis-deocata-bred/",
      "html": "<p>Clear running waters at the foot of the Himalaya.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "maintenance",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/21-seahorses-and-pipefish/microphis-deocata-bred/",
      "html": "<p>It is advisable to keep this subtropical species occasionally outdoors (balcony aquarium, special garden pond). The natural food and the sunlight are very good for the animals.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/21-seahorses-and-pipefish/microphis-deocata-bred/",
      "html": "<p>A food specialist that requires live food. It prefers mayfly larvae (closest to natural food), but also eats different mosquito larvae.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/21-seahorses-and-pipefish/microphis-deocata-bred/",
      "html": "<p>Females have a fantastic, colourful belly sail, which is carried indented under the belly during the day.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/21-seahorses-and-pipefish/microphis-deocata-bred/",
      "html": "<p>The species can be bred quite well. The animals become sexually mature when half grown, at approximately 8 cm. They are then not yet as colourful as full-grown specimens of approximately 15 cm, which often have a wonderful green shimmer.</p>"
    }
  ],
